  "statement": "Find the smallest positive integer \\(n\\) such that \\(\\underbrace{2^{2 \\cdot 2}}_{n}>3^{3^{3^{3}}}\\). (The notation \\(\\underbrace{2^{2 \\cdot 2^{2}}}_{n}\\) is used to denote a power tower with \\(n 2\\) 's. For example, \\(\\underbrace{2^{2^{2}}}_{n}\\) with \\(n=4\\) would equal \\(2^{2^{2^{2}}}\\).)",
  "answerChoices": [],
